<%#
  ONE REAL SUBFOLDER of the project's folder, recursively — a section per subfolder, nested exactly
  as it sits on disk (stage 3, S3-1; "the folder is the truth" replaces the old role-derived
  grouping). A working tree renders here too, entered rather than stopped at
  (Maker::ProjectFolderListing#tree): its own files list and its own subfolders nest the same as
  any other folder, plus a link to its commit and history pages — a repository is a section now,
  and the old standalone Repositories group (_repo_group.html.erb) is gone.

  @generated_ids IS FILTERED OUT HERE, AT EVERY LEVEL of the recursion, so a file with an addon
  origin renders ONCE, in the Generated group below, never inside the folder it happens to sit in
  (ProjectsController#show resolves @generated from @listing.node_ids, which already covers every
  depth of this tree).

  ALWAYS OPEN: S2-2's "closed by default" rule belongs to the synthetic, cross-cutting Backups
  group alone (_attachment_group.html.erb, unchanged) — a REAL subfolder is not that, whatever a
  user happens to name it.

  Local: dir (Maker::ProjectFolderListing::Dir).
%>
<% visible = dir.files.reject { |row| @generated_ids.include?(row.node_id) } %>
<section class="attachment-group file-tree-section">
  <details open>
    <%# THE NAME AND THE COUNT STAY ON ONE SOURCE LINE, WITH ONE LITERAL SPACE BETWEEN THEM —
        _attachment_group.html.erb's summary does the same, and for the same reason: a conditional
        badge/link block on its own line leaves a newline-plus-indentation TEXT NODE behind even
        when it renders nothing, which breaks a `text: /name \(N\)/` substring match against the
        rendered summary (found by driving a real request, not by reading the template). %>
    <summary class="attachment-group-head"><%= dir.name %><% if dir.repo? %> <span class="badge">repo</span><% end %> <span class="muted">(<%= visible.size %>)</span><% if dir.repo? %> <%= link_to "Commits", repo_commit_path(dir.node_id), class: "linkbtn small" %> <%= link_to "History", repo_history_path(dir.node_id), class: "linkbtn small" %><% end %></summary>
    <% if visible.any? %>
      <% if @view == "list" %>
        <%= render "file_rows", rows: visible %>
      <% else %>
        <div class="attachments-grid">
          <%= render partial: "file_tile", collection: visible, as: :row %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
    <%= render partial: "file_tree_section", collection: dir.children, as: :dir %>
  </details>
</section>
